  "manifest_sha256": "7294e3edcd3468aeb8881182f77a3f22c9d9de41dff1dba8f183e9fe1753c9a7",
  "messages": [
    {
      "content": "Solve this problem step by step. Put your final answer within \\boxed{}.\n\nHow many shrimp can Emily peel and saute in ten minutes? Emily can peel 7 shrimp per minute. Emily has 100 unpeeled shrimp available. Emily works continuously for the entire ten-minute period.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Emily peels:\n\n\\[\n7 \\text{ shrimp/minute} \\times 10 \\text{ minutes}=70\\text{ shrimp}.\n\\]\n\nSince 70 is less than the 100 shrimp available, she can peel and saute:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{70\\text{ shrimp}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Wait, I made a mistake. Emily can peel 6 shrimp per minute.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Emily can peel:\n\n\\[\n6\\text{ shrimp/minute}\\times 10\\text{ minutes}=60\\text{ shrimp}.\n\\]\n\nSince 60 is fewer than the 100 available, she can peel and sauté:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{60\\text{ shrimp}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Okay, now let me ask about just one part of that. How many shrimp can Emily peel in ten minutes? Additionally, Emily discards 5 shrimp after peeling them because they are damaged.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Emily peels:\n\n\\[\n6\\text{ shrimp/minute}\\times 10\\text{ minutes}=60\\text{ shrimp}.\n\\]\n\nShe discards 5 damaged shrimp:\n\n\\[\n60-5=55.\n\\]\n\nThus, Emily peels \\(\\boxed{60\\text{ shrimp}}\\), of which \\(\\boxed{55\\text{ shrimp}}\\) remain usable.",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "I should also tell you: Emily can saute 30 shrimp in 12 minutes.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "In 10 minutes, Emily can:\n\n- Peel \\(6 \\times 10 = 60\\) shrimp.\n- Discard 5 damaged shrimp, leaving \\(60-5=55\\) usable shrimp.\n- Sauté \\(\\frac{30}{12}\\times 10=25\\) shrimp.\n\nTherefore, the sautéing capacity limits her to:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{25\\text{ shrimp}}\n\\]\n\nShe can peel 60 shrimp, but only 25 can be sautéed in ten minutes.",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Actually, that was wrong. Emily can saute 30 shrimp in 10 minutes.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Emily can peel:\n\n\\[\n6 \\times 10=60\\text{ shrimp}.\n\\]\n\nAfter discarding 5 damaged shrimp:\n\n\\[\n60-5=55\\text{ usable shrimp}.\n\\]\n\nShe can sauté 30 shrimp in 10 minutes, so the sautéing capacity limits her to:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{30\\text{ shrimp}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Here's another detail: Emily peels and sautes each shrimp sequentially rather than simultaneously.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Since Emily works on each shrimp sequentially:\n\n- Peeling one shrimp takes \\(\\frac{1}{6}\\) minute.\n- Sautéing one shrimp takes \\(\\frac{1}{3}\\) minute, since \\(30\\) take \\(10\\) minutes.\n\nThus, each shrimp takes\n\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{6}+\\frac{1}{3}\n=\\frac{1}{2}\\text{ minute}.\n\\]\n\nIn 10 minutes, she can process\n\n\\[\n\\frac{10}{1/2}=20\\text{ shrimp}.\n\\]\n\nAfter discarding 5 damaged shrimp:\n\n\\[\n20-5=15.\n\\]\n\nTherefore, Emily can sauté \\(\\boxed{15\\text{ shrimp}}\\).",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "GOOD: —\nBAD: —\nWATCH: \"Here's another detail: Emily peels and s\"",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Got it. But now I only need to know about: How long will it take Emily to peel and cook the shrimp? By the way, Emily needs to peel and cook 90 shrimp.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "To cook 90 usable shrimp, Emily must first peel 90 shrimp and account for the 5 damaged shrimp she discards. Thus, she must peel:\n\n\\[\n90+5=95\\text{ shrimp}.\n\\]\n\nBecause she peels and sautés sequentially:\n\n- Peeling time:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{95}{6}=15\\frac{5}{6}\\text{ minutes}\n\\]\n\n- Sautéing time:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{90}{30/10}=30\\text{ minutes}\n\\]\n\nTotal time:\n\n\\[\n15\\frac{5}{6}+30=45\\frac{5}{6}\\text{ minutes}.\n\\]\n\nTherefore, it will take Emily \\(\\boxed{45\\frac{5}{6}\\text{ minutes}}\\), or approximately \\(\\boxed{45\\text{ minutes }50\\text{ seconds}}\\).",
      "role": "assistant"
    }
  ],
